// A validation failure is misuse -> unchecked
class InvalidOrderException extends RuntimeException {
    InvalidOrderException(String message) { super(message); }
}

Order validate(Order o) {
    if (o.items().isEmpty())
        throw new InvalidOrderException("order must have items");
    return o;
}
Order place(Order o) { return validate(o); }   // no throws clutter
orders.forEach(this::place);                    // composes in streams
```
*Reserve checked for the rare failure a caller can genuinely recover from.*

```java
public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) { super(message); }
}

@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException e) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                .body(new ApiError(404, e.getMessage()));
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(ValidationException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ApiError> handleValidation(ValidationException e) {
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body(new ApiError(400, e.getMessage()));
    }
}
```
*One place owns HTTP status mapping; controllers and services throw plain domain exceptions.*

```java
public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    private final String resourceType;   // structured context
    private final Object resourceId;

    public ResourceNotFoundException(String resourceType, Object resourceId) {
        super(resourceType + " not found: " + resourceId);  // human message
        this.resourceType = resourceType;
        this.resourceId = resourceId;
    }
    public String getResourceType() { return resourceType; }
    public Object getResourceId()   { return resourceId; }
}

// A handler can now build a precise response without parsing the message:
// new ApiError("NOT_FOUND", e.getResourceType(), e.getResourceId())
```
*Fields carry machine-usable context; the `super(...)` message stays the human-readable summary.*

```java
public class PaymentException extends RuntimeException {
    // Version stamp for the serialized form; silences the compiler warning
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;

    public PaymentException(String message) { super(message); }
    public PaymentException(String message, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, cause);
    }
}
```
*Pick any constant (commonly `1L`) and keep it fixed; only bump it if you intentionally break serialization compatibility.*
